<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Cape Matapan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">27–29 March <a href="/years/1941">1941</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Cape Matapan was a naval battle fought on 27–29 March 1941 off the south-western coast of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, between the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> Fleet under Admiral Andrew Cunningham and the Italian navy. Helped by intercepted signals and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/radar">radar</a>, the British sank three Italian heavy cruisers and two destroyers at night, killing some 2,300 Italian sailors. Afterwards the Italian fleet avoided challenging the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy</a> in the eastern Mediterranean.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-cape-matapan.jpg" alt="Battle of Cape Matapan" width="320" height="203" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NavalHistory at English Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Cape_Matapan_map.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In the Second World War, from June 1940, Italian forces were defeated in Greece and North Africa, lost ships at Taranto and <b>Cape Matapan</b>, and suffered heavy losses on the Don in 1942–1943.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-italy">Kingdom of Italy · Military</a></li></ul></section>
